cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "USearchMolecules: An Open, Searchable Atlas of Chemical and Biological Entities"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/unum-science/USearchMolecules
url: https://ashvardanian.com/posts/usearch-molecules/
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21613663
abstract: >-
  USearchMolecules is an open, searchable atlas of chemical and biological entities, from the
  small molecules people make, screen and buy to the proteins they target and the antibodies that
  bind them. Every entity is one Parquet row under a permanent key derived from the entity itself,
  so a compound or a sequence keeps one key across collections and releases, while fingerprints,
  conformers, predicted structures and germline calls are added beside the same rows together
  with USearch graphs that link each entity to its nearest neighbors. It is distributed as
  row-aligned Parquet shards and graph files in a public S3 bucket readable without an account,
  for chemists, biologists, retrieval pipelines and agents that search across billions of entities.
keywords:
  - cheminformatics
  - bioinformatics
  - molecular similarity search
  - molecular fingerprint
  - protein structure
  - antibody repertoire
  - vector search
  - open data

